      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-157276",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the function $f(x)$, defined as\n\n$f(x) = \\frac{\\sin x - x}{x^{2} - x\\cos x}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The function is decreasing on $x \u2208 (-2,-1)$\n2. Rounded to three decimal places, $f^{\u2032}(-2) \\approx - 0.255$\n3. Rounded to three decimal places, $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^{-1}f(x)dx \\approx 0.217$\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
