      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-157279",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the function $f(x)$, defined as\n$f(x) = \\frac{xe^{\\sin x} + 1}{x}$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The function is increasing on $x \u2208 (-4,-2)$\n2. Rounded to three decimal places, $f^{\u2032}(-3) \\approx - 0.971$\n3. Rounded to three decimal places, $\\displaystyle \\int_{-4}^{-2}f(x)dx \\approx 1.241$\n\n> A graphing calculator is required to answer this question."
